{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792508266,"nonce":"9Y770o7O5DpKjturbuWp6W0xkM0=","message":"Implemented in 6fe86e2229664aedffac5604c866fa42b3c163b9.\n\nModuleId interns the logical identity and its native prefix. parse_program uses the supplied source identity; parse_module accepts a canonical identity separately from the diagnostic filename, and zynode canonicalizes its input path. Function names, lifted arrows, generated bindings and physical record names share that namespace. Identity and source-name components use an injective linker-safe encoding, including underscores, dollar signs, punctuation and Unicode. The lowerer retains one reusable name buffer with the prefix already written; it does not clone typed programs or HIR to qualify names. ModuleId::function_name gives hosts and shared linkers the same identity used by the frontend.\n\nThe registry and initializer carry the logical origin. TypedFunction.module remains reserved for imported declarations under the shared lowering convention; the import chain supplies it when a declaration crosses that boundary. Runtime extern symbols and source property names remain unchanged.\n\nRegression coverage links separately parsed libraries with the same function names and different record layouts, callback bodies and typed-array operations, both directly through CompiledImport and through shared lowered snapshots. Interpreter-first execution, mixed interpreter/Cranelift and Cranelift/LLVM execution, and full native promotion preserve both libraries' results. Source HIR retains direct float GEPs and static record/header/buffer releases. Snapshot checks keep concrete bodies deferred rather than forcing decoding to inspect them. A pinned Node/TypeScript case executes Unicode and escape-like source identifiers.\n\nValidation:\n- 54/54 TypeScript Rust tests with default features.\n- 54/54 with llvm-backend and allocation-audit; two allocation profiles intentionally ignored in the full suite.\n- The unused snapshot template allocation regression passes when run separately, preserving encoded unused bodies and the selective decode budget.\n- 645/645 conformance runs: 215 fixtures across interpreter, Cranelift and LLVM profiles. The new identifier case also passes the live TypeScript 6.0.2/Node oracle in all three profiles.\n- Clippy for all TypeScript targets with LLVM/allocation features and -D warnings, cargo fmt --all --check and git diff --check pass.\n- No KNOWN_FAILURES additions.\n\nThis closes native symbol identity only. TypeScript import/export syntax, resolution, exported checker/ownership interfaces and full module semantics remain in 0c26889a7cd2c4060eb94ef93fd808c2857089dbf714735ca52b5d071bdb1564.","files":null}]}